    "goal": "Recapitulate venular wall shear at the lower end of the physiological microvascular range (1 dyn/cm² = 0.1 Pa) in a perfused HUVEC microchannel.",
    "rationale": "Target shear 1 dyn/cm² = 0.1 Pa is the lower bound of the microvascular/venular endothelial shear range (0.1–1 Pa, per HUVEC physiology registry). A 400 µm × 100 µm × 20 mm PDMS channel at 4.0 µL/min (viscosity 1e-3 Pa·s) yields exactly 0.1 Pa wall shear (verified via flow_rate_for_shear_stress and wall_shear_stress). Reynolds ≈ 0.27 (firmly laminar), pressure drop ≈ 40 Pa (well within syringe-pump range), residence time ≈ 12 s. HUVEC seeded at 15,000 cells/cm² (mid-range of 10–20k) on the 0.08 cm² channel floor ≈ 1200 cells. Culture medium viscosity assumed water-like (1e-3 Pa·s).",
